{#
  GALLERY, every photograph we have, by job.

  THE ONE PAGE THAT IS ONLY PICTURES. Everywhere else a photograph is cropped
  to a band, a card or a frame and asked to carry copy; here each one is shown
  as it was taken, 3:2, with nothing over it. The point of the page is proof:
  the plant rooms, the kiosks and the vans are ours, on jobs we did, which is
  the difference between a firm that installs these systems and a firm that has
  a website about them.

  GROUPED BY JOB rather than by subject, because that is how the client
  supplied them and because "this house, these rooms, this kiosk in the field"
  tells the story of a supply the way a wall of blue vessels cannot. Each job
  gets a short header (name, place, one line on what it was) and then a bento
  of its photographs: the lead shot two columns wide and two rows tall, the
  rest at single size beside and below it. Every picture is the same 3:2, so
  two single cards stack to exactly the height of one lead card and the grid
  closes without gaps.

  DATA. Everything comes from _data/photos.js: names, places, the one-line
  notes, the alt text, and which picture leads. Adding a photograph is one row
  there and nothing here. The grid serves the 960px copies in /assets/gallery/
  at single size and the full 1536px file on the lead card, which is the only
  one wide enough to need it.

  NO LIGHTBOX. It was considered and dropped: it is a second component to
  maintain for a page whose cards already show a 3:2 frame at up to 800px wide,
  and the first thing a lightbox does is hide the other eleven pictures.

  NAMES follow the case-study rule: initials as the client supplied them,
  places at town or county level. See the note in photos.js on U Farm.
#}
    <!-- ===================== HERO (dark) ===================== -->
    <section class="section gallery-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="eyebrow gallery-hero__eyebrow">Gallery</p>
        <h1 class="statement gallery-hero__title">The work, <span class="em">as it is on site.</span></h1>
        <p class="gallery-hero__lead">Plant rooms, boreholes, control panels and the houses they serve. Every photograph here is from one of our own jobs, taken by us.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===================== JOBS (light) ===================== -->
    <section class="section section--light gallery" aria-label="Photographs by job">
      <div class="container">
        {% for job in photos %}
        {% if job.photos and job.photos.length %}
        {#- The lead is the photograph flagged `lead`, else the first. It is pulled
            to the front so the grid's first cell is always the wide one. -#}
        {% set lead = null %}
        {% for p in job.photos %}{% if p.lead and not lead %}{% set lead = p %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
        {% if not lead %}{% set lead = job.photos[0] %}{% endif %}
        {% set rest = [] %}
        {% for p in job.photos %}{% if p.src != lead.src %}{% set _ = rest.push(p) %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
        <article class="gallery-job" id="{{ job.id }}" aria-labelledby="gallery-job-{{ job.id }}">
          <header class="gallery-job__head">
            <div class="gallery-job__name">
              <h2 id="gallery-job-{{ job.id }}">{{ job.name }}</h2>
              {% if job.place %}<p class="gallery-job__place">{{ job.place }}</p>{% endif %}
            </div>
            {% if job.note %}<p class="gallery-job__note">{{ job.note }}</p>{% endif %}
            <p class="gallery-job__count numeral" aria-hidden="true">{{ job.photos.length }} {{ "photograph" if job.photos.length == 1 else "photographs" }}</p>
          </header>

          <ul class="gallery__grid gallery__grid--{{ job.photos.length }}" role="list">
            <li class="gallery__cell gallery__cell--lead">
              <figure class="gallery__card">
                <img src="{{ lead.src }}" alt="{{ lead.alt }}" width="1536" height="1024" loading="{{ 'eager' if loop.first else 'lazy' }}" decoding="async">
              </figure>
            </li>
            {% for p in rest %}
            <li class="gallery__cell">
              <figure class="gallery__card">
                <img src="{{ p.src | replace('/assets/', '/assets/gallery/') }}" alt="{{ p.alt }}" width="960" height="640" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
              </figure>
            </li>
            {% endfor %}
          </ul>
        </article>
        {% endif %}
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===================== COVERAGE BAND =====================
      Closes the page the way it closes every service page and /about/: after
      the pictures of where we have been, where we can come to.
    -->
    {% include "coverage-band.njk" %}
